\paragraph{Execution Environment.}
The GPU availability campaign (RQ4) is executed on a Google Cloud Platform
node equipped with one @GPU_NAME@ GPU and approximately
@GPU_VRAM_MIB@\,MiB of GDDR6 memory (UUID: \texttt{@GPU_UUID@}).
The host operating system is @OS_VERSION@ with NVIDIA driver~@NVIDIA_DRIVER@.
PyTorch~@PYTORCH_VERSION@ is installed with CUDA runtime~@PYTORCH_CUDA_RUNTIME@;
the specific CUDA wheel is selected at deployment time based on driver
compatibility rather than being hard-coded.

\paragraph{Reproducibility Controls.}
Model weights are pinned to immutable Hugging Face Hub revisions:
\texttt{openai-community/gpt2} at commit
\texttt{607a30d783dfa663caf39e06633721c8d4cfcd7e} (full model) and
\texttt{sshleifer/tiny-gpt2} at commit
\texttt{5f91d94bd9cd7190a9f3216ff93cd1dd95f2c7be} (quick validation).
GPU name validation, VRAM thresholds, and safety limits are read from
\texttt{config/profiles/gpu.yaml} at runtime rather than hard-coded
in scripts.

\paragraph{Provenance.}
Campaign identifier: \texttt{@CAMPAIGN_ID@}.
Source commit: \texttt{@SOURCE_COMMIT@}.
